<title>HONG KONG: Int'l Pipe proposes to change name.</title>
<headline>Int'l Pipe proposes to change name.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Concrete pipes manufacturer International Pipe Ltd said on Monday it proposed to change its name to K. Wah Construction Materials Ltd.</p>
<p>The name change was subject to shareholder approval in an extraordinary general meeting of the company to be beld on May 22, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The proposal was made after its parent K. Wah International Holdings Ltd announced a group restructuring plan in February to streamline its business by injecting two construction materials units into the company.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (842) 2843 6369</p>
